---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const description="Foragers cross three resource ecologies and return to the first. A fixed policy, a memory table, bounded mutation and matched random search face the same weather cues and pay the same field-calibration cost. An unseen evaluator keeps the score.";
const path='/intelligence/agent-swarm/learn-forget-evolve/';
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'LearningResource',name:"Learn, Forget, Evolve",description,url:'https://iamrobin.ai'+path,learningResourceType:'Interactive simulation',inLanguage:'en'};
const content="<div class=\"swarm-lab\"><a class=\"lab-back\" href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/\">← Agent Swarm Lab</a><p class=\"lab-kicker\">Field study 03 / 06 · Learn, Forget, Evolve</p><header class=\"lab-head\"><h1>Learn a world.<br><em>Lose a world.</em></h1><p class=\"lab-deck\">A policy that worked yesterday may be precisely the wrong habit tomorrow. The old world will come back to check.</p></header><p class=\"lab-zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">学会一个世界，也可能遗忘一个世界。</p><section class=\"lab-stage\" data-swarm-model=\"/agent-swarm/learn-forget-evolve/\" aria-label=\"Learn, Forget, Evolve interactive simulator\">\n <div class=\"lab-stage-top\"><span><i class=\"lab-live-dot\"></i>OBSERVATORY / 03</span><span>Seeded simulation · evaluator view</span></div>\n <div class=\"lab-grid\"><div class=\"lab-view\"><canvas class=\"lab-world\" data-world aria-label=\"Animated orthographic 3D sketch of simulator states. Current and final measures are available in the table below.\"></canvas><div class=\"lab-camera\"><button type=\"button\" data-camera>Plan / 3D</button><button type=\"button\" data-rotate>Rotate ↻</button></div></div>\n <aside class=\"lab-side\"><label>Treatment<select data-arm aria-label=\"Treatment\"></select></label><div class=\"lab-readout\"><strong data-live-value>—</strong><span data-live-label>Delivered useful work</span></div><p class=\"lab-event\" data-event>Observe. Compare. Change one assumption.</p><p class=\"small\">Lines = recorded movement / messages · cross = failed body.</p><div class=\"lab-checks\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-compare/>Compare all</label><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-trails checked/>Trails</label><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-signals checked/>Links</label></div><label>Inspect a body<select data-agent aria-label=\"Agent to inspect\"></select></label><div class=\"lab-inspect\" data-inspect><p class=\"small\">Click a body in the world, or choose it here. This is an evaluator view of recorded state.</p></div></aside></div>\n <div class=\"lab-buttons\"><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" data-play aria-pressed=\"false\">Play world</button><button type=\"button\" data-replay>Replay ↺</button><button type=\"button\" data-end>Final tick →</button><button type=\"button\" data-next-seed>Next seed</button><button type=\"button\" data-download>Save this run ↓</button></div>\n <label class=\"lab-timeline\"><span class=\"tiny\">Time</span><input data-timeline aria-label=\"Simulation timeline\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"100\" value=\"0\"/><output data-time>0 ticks</output></label>\n <p class=\"lab-status\" data-status role=\"status\">Loading the model. Recorded evidence remains available below.</p>\n <div class=\"lab-controls\"><div><label>Choose a world<select data-preset aria-label=\"World preset\"></select></label><p data-preset-note></p><button type=\"button\" data-apply>Run these parameters →</button></div><form class=\"lab-params\" data-params aria-label=\"World parameters\"></form></div>\n <div class=\"lab-scores\"><p class=\"tiny\">Delivered useful work / units · higher is better</p><canvas data-curve class=\"lab-curve\" aria-label=\"Measured outcome over time for each treatment. Dashed markers identify interventions.\"></canvas><div class=\"lab-table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th>Treatment</th><th>At this tick</th><th>At mission end</th></tr></thead><tbody data-scores></tbody></table></div></div>\n <noscript><p>JavaScript is needed to run the simulator. Read the saved multi-seed evidence and method below.</p></noscript>\n </section>\n <section class=\"lab-section\"><p class=\"tiny\">01 / Try to break it</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>Wait for the first world to return.</h2><p>Follow A → B → C → A. Compare frozen rules, explicit memory, bounded mutation and random search. A quick recovery is interesting; a recovery that still wins after paying for calibration is more interesting. Inspect the rejected candidates too.</p><blockquote class=\"lab-hypothesis\">Can a small policy change adapt to a new world without erasing the old one?</blockquote></div></section>\n <section class=\"lab-section\"><p class=\"tiny\">02 / The mechanism</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>What the little world actually does.</h2><p>Agents operate a small, fixed policy language. Adaptation spends field trials on calibration and selection. Mutation and random search receive matched candidate budgets. Candidates face held-back calibration gates. A separate frozen evaluator audits retained policies on disjoint seeds without controlling promotion; the agent cannot rewrite its reward. A lineage records proposals, rejected candidates, promotions and rollback.</p><p>This is policy evolution inside a bounded simulator. Foundation-model weights do not change, and the experiment does not establish recursive intelligence. The useful question is smaller and testable: does experience buy better action in a changed or unseen world, after charging for it?</p><p lang=\"zh-Hans\" class=\"lab-zh\">任务按 A→B→C→A 改变，比较固定规则、明确记忆、有界变异与等预算随机搜索。训练和筛选都收费，保留的校准样本决定候选是否晋级，独立种子评估器随后审计，并记录被拒绝的候选与回滚。这是有界策略演化，不是模型权重自我进化。</p></div></section>\n <section class=\"lab-section\"><p class=\"tiny\">03 / Recorded evidence</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>Keep the inconvenient outcomes.</h2><p><strong>Simple memory won the clear-season comparison: 1,149.5 delivered units versus 931.0 for bounded mutation. Mutation also spent 6,132 training evaluations, while memory made 192 table updates; separate diagnostic evaluations are counted too. The retention criterion failed when environmental cues became ambiguous.</strong></p><p>Bounded mutation plus a retention gate may preserve useful behavior, but a simple context memory can be better, and no policy can identify hidden seasons when their observable cues become indistinguishable.</p><p class=\"small\">Paired seeded simulations. Every retained result can be regenerated from the versioned source; these are synthetic experiments, not field validation.</p><details class=\"lab-batch\"><summary>Inspect every world and treatment</summary><div class=\"lab-table-scroll\"><table><caption class=\"tiny\">Delivered useful work · mean by predeclared world</caption><thead><tr><th>World / treatment</th><th>Mean units</th><th>n</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Four seasons / Fixed habit</th><td>754.85</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Four seasons / Experience memory</th><td>1,149.55</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Four seasons / Mutation + retention gate</th><td>930.97</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Four seasons / Matched random search</th><td>864.77</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Foggy cues / Fixed habit</th><td>754.85</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Foggy cues / Experience memory</th><td>1,015.28</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Foggy cues / Mutation + retention gate</th><td>738.41</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Foggy cues / Matched random search</th><td>723.04</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Indistinguishable / Fixed habit</th><td>754.85</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Indistinguishable / Experience memory</th><td>732.2</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Indistinguishable / Mutation + retention gate</th><td>613.42</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Indistinguishable / Matched random search</th><td>519.97</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Changed home / Fixed habit</th><td>485.43</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Changed home / Experience memory</th><td>996.29</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Changed home / Mutation + retention gate</th><td>768.52</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Changed home / Matched random search</th><td>799.61</td><td>24</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><p class=\"small\">One chosen seed is an illustration. The downloadable batch retains every world and treatment; null means unavailable. A confidence interval describes the sampled synthetic worlds, not the real world.</p><div class=\"lab-links\"><a href=\"/agent-swarm/learn-forget-evolve/results.json\" download>All recorded runs ↓</a><a href=\"/agent-swarm/learn-forget-evolve/README.md\">Method &amp; reproduction</a><a href=\"/agent-swarm/learn-forget-evolve/model.mjs\">Read the model</a><a href=\"/agent-swarm/learn-forget-evolve/source.zip\" download>Source package ↓</a></div></div></section>\n <section class=\"lab-section lab-method\"><p class=\"tiny\">04 / Inspect the boundary</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>Enough detail to disagree.</h2><details><summary>Inputs, budgets and observation boundaries</summary><dl data-audit></dl></details><details><summary>Every measure in the current run</summary><div class=\"lab-table-scroll\" data-summary></div></details><ul><li>A finite contextual foraging task and a 12-parameter linear policy; not open-ended self-improvement or AGI.</li><li>Field calibration deliberately grants every arm the same paid, full-feedback resource samples. Real robots would need to collect those samples.</li><li>Policy candidates are scored on recorded calibration trials; this is not free counterfactual access to unobserved actions.</li><li>The final evaluator uses disjoint seeds and new weather samples, but the same declared family of three ecologies.</li><li>The illustrated height is a resource/learning cue, not simulated three-dimensional physics.</li></ul><p class=\"small\">3D sketching adds depth to the explanation. It does not add an unmodeled physical dimension, extra sensor data or unearned intelligence to the experiment.</p></div></section><nav class=\"lab-next\"><a href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/shared-reality/\">← Shared Reality</a><a href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/asteroid-button/\">The Asteroid Button →</a></nav></div>";
---
<BaseLayout title="Learn, Forget, Evolve — Agent Swarm Lab — Robin Xie" {path} {description} {schema}>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/agent-swarm/lab.css"/>
<Fragment set:html={content}/>
<script is:inline type="module" src="/agent-swarm/client.mjs"></script>
</BaseLayout>
